
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/d3d12/ns-d3d12-d3d12_input_layout_desc

Use it to tell PSO what the "schema" and "layout" of your Vertex Buffer looks like (IA)


 - schema : How various "named" attributes are placed within the vertex buffer (think poor man's struct definition)
   This is done by giving each attribute a "semantic name" + "semantic index" along with size

 - layout : Each attribute can point to different "Input Slots" in case attributes are laid out in an interleaved manner (across different Vertex Buffers)


 
   